--- !u!114 &1419907707
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1419907705}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: babb271d50e00eb44a8ce2a602ef8906, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoreManager
  entries:
  - title: The Workshop
    body: I only remember the smell of the workshop - porcelain dust and something
      sweet, and the bodies, empty, as if waiting, and one had a face cracked in
      half, like mine
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: The Hilt
    body: No name came back, but my hands clenched on the hilt by themselves - so
      I did something, good or bad, when the body doesn't remember pain
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: The Blue Lantern
    body: While the lantern burns - I'm stronger, and when it dies - I'm less, as
      if part of me stayed under the light, waiting not for me but for who I was
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: The Weeper
    body: The Weeper wept behind the wall for three days, didn't attack, and when
      I came close - went silent and looked as if he knew me, and I killed him before
      I could think, because my hands remembered, and he was human, and I think we
      knew each other
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: The Noise
    body: 'The dark beyond the circle of light isn''t emptiness, it''s a queue of
      those I didn''t save: they''re more patient than me and fear nothing, because
      they have nothing left to lose - and I do'
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: The Price of a Step
    body: The soul isn't what saves you, it's what you give away for a strike, for
      a step, for the chance not to think of who you were, and the more you give,
      the less remains of the one who walks
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: You Will Be the First
    body: 'By the iron door I found a shard of glass - my face, no, not mine, a doll''s
      - and remembered a voice: "You will be the first," and someone''s hands on
      my shoulders, gentle, as with a tool'
    isUnlocked: 0
  - title: Downward
    body: I  went down to find the cause and found myself, and now I'm not sure the
      cause can be forgiven, but I no longer know how to go up - up there is light,
      people, a name, and I'm only hands that remember weapons
    isUnlocked: 0
